course: dictionary
lesson: 4589
title: Henry: a name and a unit
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you something before you read them, and a capital letter is one of those clues. «Henry» with a capital H is a name, the name of a boy or a man. «Henry Ford's moving assembly line, started in 1913, made cars cheap enough for many families.» Here Henry is a person's name.
explain: «Henry in Gloucestershire hears he's going to boarding school next year» uses Henry as a boy's name too, and the capital letter shows it. Names always start with a capital, so write Henry, not henry.
explain: Now look at «a henry» with a small h. In advanced science, a henry is a unit for measuring inductance in electric coils. It is named after a scientist. Context matters: if the sentence talks about coils, currents or science, a henry is a unit, not a person.
explain: Context clues can also tell you which Henry is meant. «Henry VIII was tall, strong and sporty as a young king» is about a king, because kings were often called Henry in English history. The number VIII shows which king.
fact: Henry is a first name for a boy or a man, and it is sometimes used as a family name.
fact: Names start with a capital letter, so write Henry, not henry.
fact: «Henry VIII» was a king of England who had six wives.
fact: A henry, with a small h, is a unit for measuring inductance in electric coils.
fact: «Henry Ford's moving assembly line» cut the time to build a car from about twelve hours to about an hour and a half.
exercise: In «Henry in Gloucestershire hears he's going to boarding school next year», what kind of word is Henry? | A type of school | A place | *A name | A unit of measure
exercise: «Henry VIII was tall, strong and sporty as a young king.» Which Henry is this? | *King Henry VIII | A boy called Henry at boarding school | A henry, a unit for measuring coils | Henry Ford
exercise: Which sentence uses a henry as a science unit? | Henry Ford built cars | Henry went to school next year | *The coil measured three henries | King Henry ruled for many years
test: Why does «Henry» have a capital letter in «Henry Ford's moving assembly line»? | It is a very important word | It is the first word of the lesson | *It is a person's name, so it starts with a capital letter | It is a unit, so it always has a capital
test: Which of these is a unit for measuring inductance in electric coils? | Henry the Eighth | Henry Ford | *a henry | King Henry
exam: The children read «Henry VIII was tall, strong and sporty» and «a henry measures inductance». Which Henry is the name and which is the unit? | The first is a unit and the second is a name | Both are names | *The first is a name and the second is a unit | Both are units
